{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,175p' host/gambit/boot.ss && sed -n '1,100p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795215000000-engineer-p1f-dht-gambit-fix.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":";; boot.ss — the G2/G3 boot: the curated jolt runtime subset + the cross-minted\n;; compiler seed load on native gsi (Gambit 4.9.7). jolt-mj95.3/.4.\n;;\n;; ONE compilation unit: everything is ##include-spliced (NOT load'd) so the\n;; shim macros from prelude-shims.ss (define-record-type, fx aliases,\n;; with-mutex, ...) expand in the SAME unit as every manifest file — the\n;; \"compile the boot files together\" flow (see gambitcheck.ss's splice note).\n;;\n;; LOAD SHIM: rt.ss orchestrates its own loads ((load \"host/chez/...\") for the\n;; whole manifest plus the excluded java tail). Under this boot every manifest\n;; file is spliced in here and the excluded ones are deliberately skipped, so\n;; a runtime (load \"host/chez/...\") must be a no-op — re-loading the Chez\n;; copies would clobber the gambit sa-runtime/hasheq and pull in Chez-only\n;; java interop. vendor/irregex is NOT under host/chez and loads normally.\n(define %gambit-load load)\n(define (load path . rest)\n  (if (and (string? path)\n           (or (string-prefix? \"host/chez/\" path)\n               ;; irregex is ##include'd below (the js target has no\n               ;; filesystem — a runtime load cannot work there)\n               (string-prefix? \"vendor/irregex/\" path)))\n      #f\n      (apply %gambit-load path rest)))\n\n(##include \"prelude-shims.ss\")\n(##include \"scheme-adapter-runtime.ss\")\n\n;; ---- manifest, in rt.ss load order (findings doc, curated) ----------------\n;;\n;; G2-booted: values, hasheq(gambit), collections, seq, then rt-core (the gambit\n;; kernel — the rt.ss port; its port-log is in the file header). STOPS at the\n;; first file whose blocker is class (c) (a genuine Chez-only construct with no\n;; gambit seam) — see REPORT.\n\n(##include \"../chez/values.ss\")\n(##include \"hasheq.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/collections.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/seq.ss\")\n;; The register-*-arm! fast-type probes are LOAD-TIME SELF-CHECKS (they run\n;; each new predicate against sample values). The jrec-cl predicate probe\n;; spins on the js target (records dispatch against probe values); the\n;; invariant these checks enforce is already proven on every Chez gate run,\n;; so this target skips the probe machinery.\n(set! reject-fast-type-claim! (lambda _ #f))\n(##include \"rt-core.ss\")\n\n;; regex needs regex-translate.ss (pure; rt.ss used to preload it from java/).\n(##include \"../../vendor/irregex/irregex.scm\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/regex-translate.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/regex.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/atoms.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/refs.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/predicates.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/converters.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/transients.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-seq.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/printing.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-coll.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-num.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/multimethods.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/jdk-interfaces.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/class-hierarchy.ss\")\n;; Gambit has no host shims that load on first reference, so the Chez lazy-shims.ss\n;; hooks the records layer asks (an unloaded class's ctor or method) answer #f.\n(define (lazy-shims-provides? name) #f)\n(define (lazy-shims-method! name) #f)\n(##include \"records-gambit.ss\")  ;; GENERATED from records.ss (make gambitgen) — phase wall, see gen-records.ss\n(##include \"../chez/java/records-interop.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-meta.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/host-class.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/dynamic-var-defaults.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/host-table.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/lazy-bridge.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-transduce.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/vars.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-misc.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-format.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/extensions.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/ns.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/dyn-binding.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/natives-reader.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/reader.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/syntax-quote.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/host-contract.ss\")\n;; The interop tier: the jhost record and the registries (host-statics.ss),\n;; then the java/ files shared with Chez that register into them — Class\n;; objects and the class model core reads (class-model.ss), StringBuilder\n;; (string-builder.ss), the `.`/`.-field` dispatch arms over records, maps and\n;; transients (dot-forms.ss). Before the seed: the prelude's own (import …) forms\n;; intern through jolt-class-for (host-vars.ss, the rest of the java/ tree's\n;; names, comes after it). java-parse.ss is the NumberFormatException family\n;; Long/parseLong and its siblings raise.\n(##include \"../chez/java/java-parse.ss\")\n(##include \"host-statics.ss\")\n;; java.lang.Math and clojure.math: one portable file, shared with Chez\n(##include \"../chez/java/math.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/class-model.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/string-builder.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/dot-forms.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/jutil-colls.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/java/tree-map.ss\")\n;; java.nio's buffers and ByteOrder, over bytevectors. The buffer array seam\n;; is excluded, so a ByteBuffer has no .array and typed buffers are views.\n(##include \"../chez/java/byte-buffer.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/float.ss\")  ;; java.lang.Float as a value (jfloat)\n(##include \"../chez/surrogates.ss\")  ;; a UTF-16 surrogate unit as a Character (jsurr)\n\n;; ---- G3: the cross-minted compiler on gsi (jolt-mj95.4) ----------------------\n;;\n;; The seed (host/gambit/seed/{prelude,image}.ss — clojure.core + the compiler,\n;; minted at :gambit by make gambitseed) is spliced HERE, BEFORE compile-eval.ss,\n;; mirroring cli.ss's load order: compile-eval.ss's top-level forms var-deref the\n;; image's vars (jolt.analyzer/analyze, jolt.backend-scheme/emit-top-form), so\n;; the image must have loaded first. Same-unit rule: all three are ##include'd —\n;; the seed's emitted code expands seq.ss's macros in this unit; a load'd seed\n;; would be a separate unit that cannot see them.\n(##include \"eval-fns.ss\")  ;; seq.ss numeric macros as eval-world FUNCTIONS (js exes cannot eval define-syntax)\n;; clojure.core is the current namespace while its own prelude loads, as in\n;; cli.ss: the prelude's defmultis (print-method) def-var! into the current ns\n;; and its (import …) forms bind class tokens there — under the default \"user\"\n;; both landed in the wrong namespace (clojure.core/Sequential stayed unbound).\n(set-chez-ns! \"clojure.core\")\n(##include \"seed/prelude.ss\")\n;; post-prelude re-asserts the native overrides the overlay stubs out (ns-name,\n;; char?, atom?, realized?, ...) — cli.ss order: prelude, post-prelude, image.\n(##include \"../chez/post-prelude.ss\")\n;; the clojure.core names the excluded java/ tree owns on Chez — after\n;; post-prelude so these bindings are the last word\n(##include \"host-vars.ss\")\n;; the jolt.ffi names the excluded java/ffi.ss owns on Chez — P1b-stage1: the\n;; memory/loader/errno surface behind the qualified tier, with every\n;; unimplemented row bound to a message-carrying refusal (same rule as\n;; host-vars.ss: nothing unbound, nothing pretending)\n(##include \"host-ffi.ss\")\n(set-chez-ns! \"user\")\n(##include \"seed/image.ss\")\n(##include \"../chez/compile-eval.ss\")\n\n;; The compiled image's compiler unit defaults to :chez (new-unit's :target); the\n;; boot must flip it to :gambit before any runtime compile, or the emitter writes\n;; #3% unsafe spellings that cannot load on gsi. set-target! (R9) resets the\n;; current unit's :target — the unit compile-eval.ss's set-prelude-mode! just\n;; created on first touch (cur() lazily populates current-unit-box).\n(let ((st (var-deref \"jolt.backend-scheme\" \"set-target!\")))\n  (if (procedure? st)\n      (begin (st (keyword #f \"gambit\")) (display \"boot: backend target -> :gambit\\n\"))\n      (begin (display \"boot: FATAL set-target! missing from seed image\\n\") (exit 1))))\n\n;; (smoke block removed — gambitkernel/gambiteval gates cover it)\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-21 18:07:05 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-22 01:07:05 ICT (+07)\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-21 17:10:21 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-22 00:10:21 ICT (+07)\nCoding-Agent: Codex (gpt-6.2-sol)\nSession-ID: 01a1ff16-8664-7961-8de5-d59245d34ee7\nRole: VM Runtime Engineer (implementation)\n\n# P1f — memory-backed dao.jing.dht on Jolt Gambit\n\nLocal branch `gambit-ffi-p1f` in `/Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1f`, based on\n`gambit-ffi-p1e` at `0aa7f8a470beeb33988583a1eaf6d069718c4bea`.\nCommitted `bbd35983ee5d5f7c3816a3fcd7540039aecbb8c4` locally. Datomworld input `533216bec2354d9263a8a17a146a3e8172b39a64`.\n\n| Blocker | Status | Implementation and evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Missing shim rows and byte copies | Fixed | `host/gambit/ffi/shapes.json:326` declares four finite tuples. `inet_pton` uses three arguments and `inet_ntop` uses four, including its destination pointer. `sendto` and `recvfrom` each use six arguments with invocation-local errno capture. The generated shims, C fixtures, source digests, and local toolchain provenance were verified. `host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-abi.ss:242` checks output pointers, wide size/result values, unsigned socklen, and errno. `host/gambit/host-ffi.ss:229` uses the existing u8vector bulk-copy bridge for two-argument `read-array` and `write-array`. |\n| Socket close | Datagram cleanup works through a native worker. Inline close stays refused. | `stdlib/jolt/socket/native.clj:267` keeps the `:blocking` binding. The Gambit datagram branch at line 615 checks the local family and socket type before calling the worker. The C worker at `host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm:98` captures the syscall result and errno immediately. It owns only C memory and the descriptor. Gambit parks between polls at line 277. `host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-abi.ss:280` checks success, verifies that the descriptor is closed, and checks the worker's EBADF. |\n| Session source `ffi/defcfn` | Fixed | `host/gambit/yin-repl-driver.ss:75` leaves only `clojure.core` in the booted set, so the source loader loads canonical `stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj`. `host/gambit/source-loader.ss:87` adds the Gambit reader feature while evaluating a source namespace. The source gate expands the canonical declaration macro at `host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss:57`. |\n| `java.io.File` | Constructor fixed. File I/O stays refused. | `host/gambit/host-statics.ss:199` registers the path constructor and `getPath`. The same shim sends `exists`, `isDirectory`, `canWrite`, and `mkdirs` to the C4 refusal. The durable store's POSIX file overlay remains behind that refusal. |\n| `ClassCastException` | Fixed | `host/chez/collections.ss:184` and `:271` check `rrbnode?` when selecting the relaxed traversal. Gambit represents an RRB record as a vector. The old dense fast path read the record's tag, `16`, and passed it to `vector-ref` as a child. P1e also recognized the plain vector `#(16 99)` as an RRB record. `host/gambit/prelude-shims.ss:100` assigns private identity tags, with the corresponding identity-hash check at `host/gambit/hasheq.ss:553`. |\n| Store admission and composition | Memory-backed `dht:` admitted. Durable `dht:<dir>` remains Chez-only. | `host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt:34` joins the portable Dao DHT node over a memory store and supplies its handle and message-derived payload budget to Yin. The CLI accepts the exact `dht:` argument at line 56. The profile opens a solo node. The loopback gate exercises the native UDP transport in that session. |\n\n## Close evidence and platform detection\n\nThe descriptor flag alone cannot prove a bounded close. Darwin's XNU close\npath checks for a content filter independently of linger, and its UDP filter\npath can wait for a filter to detach. Linux's UDP close handler calls\n`sk_common_release` without consuming the linger timeout. This evidence\nsupports keeping synchronous socket close behind C4 and using the separate\nnative worker for datagram cleanup. The worker enters no Gambit code and\nperforms no GC release or claim. [XNU socket close](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/bsd/kern/uipc_socket.c#L1040-L1073), [XNU UDP filter close](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/bsd/net/content_filter.c#L6374-L6392), [Linux UDP close](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/include/net/udp.h#L301-L304)\n\nThe Gambit OS adapter had returned Linux on every host. On Darwin that caused\nthe socket namespace to read the BSD sockaddr header as a 16-bit Linux family.\n`host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:261` derives Darwin from Gambit's\nconfigured system triple. The adapter gate compares it with the native\nbridge's compile-time platform.\n\n## Verification\n\nDarwin arm64, native Gambit 4.9.8. The stage-1 matrix passed\n`gambitffi`, `gambitcheck`, `gambitkernel`, `gambiteval`,\n`gambitgencheck`, `gambitseedcheck`, `emittedheads`, and `deadhost`.\nThe ABI gate ran 92 checks and the public FFI gate ran 50, with zero\nfailures. `gambitsourceload` also passed. The shared Chez RRB property\ngate passed 11,170 checks. Native Darwin IPv6 address conversion returned\n`[\"::1\" 12345 28]`. Linux execution is the orchestrator's follow-up.\n\n`make gambitdht` builds the bridge and compiled boot and runs both halves of\n`test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh`. In this run the stock and diagnostic halves\nran as separate foreground invocations with a 2,400-second watchdog per\nlauncher. The diagnostic copy adds one test host module around the same\nproduction store opener. The final transcript assertions were applied to\nthe original diagnostic receipt after accepting the vector delimiter\nspacing emitted by Yin. Both launchers exited 0 and the diagnostic store\ndirectory stayed empty.\n\n```text\nyin> 42\nyin> Bye\nstock launcher exit 0 (785s)\n```\n\n```text\nyin> 42\nyin> 'p1e.probe\nyin> [ :dht-index-put-get :segment/blake3-9ae30c66b5af21de9431ed9aca9a48028df9cd2df20c2f7defb74f8740110de9 {:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3} ]\nyin> Error: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)\nyin> :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle\nyin> :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle\nyin> Error: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)\nyin> :memory-dht-handle-opened\nyin> :segment/blake3-9ae30c66b5af21de9431ed9aca9a48028df9cd2df20c2f7defb74f8740110de9\nyin> {:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3}\nyin> true\nyin> [:udp-loopback-ok \"Kv8A\" :closed]\nyin> :socket-native-loaded\nyin> Error: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)\nyin> :closed\nyin> 43\nyin> Bye\ndiagnostics launcher exit 0 (2093s)\n```\n\nReceipts are under `build/gambit-dht/run.V058gh/`, `build/gambit-dht/run.TnOT3j/`, and\n`build/p1f/matrix-verified.log` in the P1f worktree.\n\nDONE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
